//! Realms, as the account library (osis-account) makes them. A realm is a thing whose holders are
//! its members, each at a role: read sees what is in it, write takes part (chats, documents) and
//! adds to it, admin also manages its members and details. In it is what it is mint admin of
//! (minted with it as mint admin: stays when the member who minted it leaves) and what it holds a grant on (shared into it).
//! Nesting, overlap and roles inside a realm are grants between realms.
//!
//! A person's account is a realm whose members are the person's nodes, each writing as its node
//! thing through it; each node names it in its node root's `settings^.0`. It is the person's
//! home: what they make is minted with it as admin and held from its `holds.0`, and their own
//! state in apps (schema/ui.osis) is on it.
revision 1;

/// Marks a realm users see, with the details only its admins change. Its name is `name.0`.
admin aspect realm:realm^.0: struct {
    /// `#rrggbb`.
    color 0: option<string>,
};

/// On a realm: its profile, what everyone may read about it (`name.0`, `contact:*`). Held by the
/// realm, public, naming the realm in `realm:of.0` and carrying the realm's card, which names
/// where grants to the realm from outside arrive: whoever holds the profile may grant the realm
/// roles. Every account has one.
aspect realm:profile.0: weak;

/// On a profile: the realm it is the profile of.
aspect realm:of.0: weak;

/// On a realm: the profiles of other realms it imported by their contact cards (each held by
/// the realm), by realm.
aspect realm:contacts.0: map<weak, weak>;
